Kristian Glass <kg289@spam.ac.uk> writes:
> Stuart Wheaton wrote:

> > When dipping in fountains and so forth, I fear the accidental capital
> > and such.  The game asks, "what do you want to dip?"  then you choose,
> > then it asks, "dip _it_ into the fountain?"
> > If it said "Dip _your foo_ into the fountain?" you'd have one last
> > chance to avoid blanking an expensive scroll or so forth...

> I'd agree, if it's going to attempt to give you a chance to confirm, it
> might as well provide useful information.
> So, trivial patch at http://www.srcf.ucam.org/~kg289/nethack/betterdip.diff

This functionality has now been added to the paranoid patch and my
combined patch, with a little enhancement:
Kristian's version only showed the name of the item to be dipped into
fountains and pools, not when you dipped something into potions. I added
showing the name also when you dip into a potion.
I felt this was something that would fit the paranoid patch, so I added it
there. I didn't add runtime options to toggle it on or off, because I
don't think anybody minds seeing the information about what is to be
dipped. At least not anybody who will use the paranoid patch.

